        "heading": "Why I started this",
        "heading_size": "h0",
        "body": "<p>I spent eleven years as a formulation chemist, most of it making products for brands whose names are on shelves you have walked past. Almost none of them were designed with India in mind.</p><p>The moment it stopped being tolerable was fairly small. A friend asked why the vitamin C serum I had helped develop had gone brown, and I had to explain that it was working exactly as designed — for a climate she does not live in. It had been sold to her anyway.</p><p>EMBRAE is the attempt to do the same job honestly. Fewer products, every dose printed, formulated for the room the bottle actually sits in. It is a slower way to build a brand and I have made peace with that.</p>",
